Name: themeChanged

Type: message

Syntax: themeChanged

Summary:
Sent to the <current card> of a <stack> when its <lightTheme> or <darkTheme>
is set.

Associations: card

Introduced: 0.9.16

OS: mac, windows, linux

Platforms: desktop

Example:
on themeChanged
   -- colors worked out by script are worked out again
   set the backgroundColor of graphic "Banner" to \
         the effective hiliteColor of this stack
   pass themeChanged
end themeChanged

Description:
Handle the <themeChanged> <message> if a script keeps colors that depend on
the stack's theme and has to work them out again when the theme changes.

Most stacks do not need it. Objects with no colors of their own are redrawn
in the new theme by the engine, and so are widgets that read their colors
while painting. The message is for controls that paint colors once and keep
them, such as a control that draws into an image, or sets the colors of its
parts by script. The Data Grid uses it to draw its rows again.

The message is sent to the current card of the stack whose <lightTheme> or
<darkTheme> was set, and to the current card of each of its open substacks,
after the handler that set the property has finished. It is sent whenever
the property is set, including when the theme is removed by setting it to
<empty>, and whichever appearance is in use at the time.

The message is not sent when the system changes between light and dark mode.
A stack with both themes changes its colors then, so a handler that keeps
theme colors should handle the <systemAppearanceChanged> message as well.

References: lightTheme (property), darkTheme (property),
systemAppearanceChanged (message), systemAppearance (property),
effective (keyword), empty (constant), stack (object),
message (glossary), current card (glossary)
